@nsobid-28C4287AEE36F7499DA60F3E68B54C70DA382D75

# Splatoon 3 11.3.0 - Double Buffering

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces a two-texture swapchain.
//
// nnMain builds the sead::GameFrameworkNx::CreateArg with isTripleBuffer
// (+0x1D) set, so the NVN window starts with 3 textures. The present path
// then switches between 2 and 3 active textures at runtime: it raises the
// count to 3 whenever a frame takes longer than the framework's threshold
// and drops back to 2 once frames are short again, and a pending request
// byte (+0x225) can force either count. Every route to 3 is closed here,
// so the CPU can run at most one frame ahead of scanout.

@enabled
// initial buffer count: isTripleBuffer read as false
04529F70 09008052   // MOV W9,#0 (was LDRB W9,[X19,#0xA5])
// slow-frame auto switch from 2 to 3 never fires
0452B424 12000014   // B to the present call (was B.LE)
// a triple-buffer request (1) selects 2, like the double-buffer request (0)
0452B43C 3F090071   // CMP W9,#2 (was CMP W9,#3)
0452B444 41008052   // MOV W1,#2 (was MOV W1,#3)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Splatoon 3's sead + spl::gfx + agl/gsys
// engine; 11.3.0 retail is symbol-stripped, so every site was located by
// structure and byte-verified against the IDB.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
